																		The Holder of Chance
															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/jack-ike" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1618170); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1618170&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608349679" alt="Jack Ike" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1618170)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/jack-ike" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1618170); return false;" >Jack Ike</a></span> <span class="odate time_1477479451 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">26 Oct 2016 10:57</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2677683">
									

<p>So, I wrote a SCP Foundation / The Holders crossover. It isn't <a href="/holder-of-the-foundation">the first</a>, but it's a more serious one.</p>
<p>Thanks to Dora, AJMansfield, Silber, AidenEldritch and everyone else who looked at the draft and gave feedback! <sub>(I'm sorry, my memory is terrible.)</sub></p>
<p>One of the big things that drove me to write this was the realisation that the main Holder's website, <a href="http://theholders.org">theholders.org</a>, had gone down (and has been for a month or two at the time of writing - it can still be viewed through the <a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20160413012929/http://theholders.org/">wayback machine</a>, though).<br />
<strong>Spoilers:</strong></p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;What&nbsp;is&nbsp;going&nbsp;on?</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Metafiction!</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>The Administrator (Adm) is meeting with the Holder of the End (En). They each serve as physical embodiments of their respective series - The Administrator represents the entire SCP Foundation, the Holder of the End represents the entire Holders series.</p>
<p>The Holders series is being forgotten (both in-universe and in reality), so En is dying. The SCP Foundation is still growing and thriving, so Adm is not at threat of this yet, but admits that at some point the Foundation will be forgotten too and he will die.</p>
<p>Adm and En compare various parts of themselves (The SCP Foundation and The Holders, respectively) to eachother, and how they were successful and failures in those regards.</p>
<p>The tale ends with En being incorporated into the SCP Foundation, so that even if he passes on he would still be remembered as long as the Foundation is. In-universe, this is achieved in two ways:<br />
1) The story of The Holder of the End/En is introduced into the Foundationverse and is classified as an anomaly (SCP-5380). The Administrator does this by making the story of The Holder of The End real in-universe, then handing a copy of the out-of-universe story to the Foundation (Procedure SAVIOUR'S ARK).<br />
2) The tale itself becomes part of the incorporation. As long as the tale stays up on the out-of-universe site (Which i hope it will, for a very long time), the Holders have a chance of being remembered and get the credit (I believe) they deserve.</p>
<p>The two tabs (SCP-5380 documentation &amp; Procedure SAVIOUR'S ARK) allow for a comparison of the two differing formats; the core story and content is the same, but the prior is presented in the familiar SCP format while the latter retains its Holders format.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;What&nbsp;is&nbsp;The&nbsp;Holders?</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Old-time&nbsp;rivals.</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>The Holders used to be viewed as the SCP Foundation's rivals. Both had identical origins (Both have unconfirmed beginnings, but are attributed to a single anonymous post on the /x/ forum of 4chan in the year 2007), both were aimed at being horror-oriented creepypastas.</p>
<p>From there though, divurgences occur; while the <a href="/scp-173">SCP-173</a> post limited the number of anomalies to a minimum of 173 but set no maximum, the first Holder post did the opposite; the maximum number of Holder items was set at 538 (some versions stated that there was 2,538 of these items, but 2,000 of them were permanently lost or destroyed). Over time, the difference between the two became more apparent. The Foundation began growing beyond simple horror, spreading to general science fiction, while the Holders remained strictly devoted to the horror origins. Their format was far more restrictive too (as explained in the tale).</p>
<p>As of late, though, they've been almost entirely forgotten. Their main site, [theholders.org] has been down for several months now and is unlikely to come back up, as the most recent edits prior were back in 2013.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Why&nbsp;'The&nbsp;Holder&nbsp;of&nbsp;The&nbsp;End'?</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Roots.</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>Simple: The Holder of The End is to the Holders as SCP-173 is to the Foundation; it was the first one made, and the one to spawn them all.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<hr />
<p><a href="http://scpfoundation.ru/holding-on">Russian translation</a> by <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/4ophbiu-6o6p" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(779782); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=779782&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1484883100" alt="4opHbIu_6o6p" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=779782)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/4ophbiu-6o6p" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(779782); return false;">4opHbIu_6o6p</a></span>!</p>

