				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/novaedearx" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1310897); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1310897&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608349679" alt="NovaeDeArx" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1310897)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/novaedearx" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1310897); return false;" >NovaeDeArx</a></span> <span class="odate time_1477692100 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">28 Oct 2016 22:01</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2679165">
									

<p>The Holders suffered from lack of quality control as well as repetition. However, there are a few gems buried in there. It's just frustrating that even as a first-time reader, one quickly (within 5-10 articles at most) gets pulled out of the stories just because you can't help but go &quot;A mental institution? Again?!&quot; and roll your eyes.</p>
<p>It's just exhausting to sort through all the samey articles, all the purple prose, and all the attempts to copy the successful articles without actually doing anything original. So sort of like reading the SCP &quot;most recent&quot; list that hasn't been filtered yet, but worse.</p>

							</div>

								
					
